A||||8||HAGS||86' Fiero SE 2m4 tips?||||5||
Z||000000||HAGS||11-03-2000||04:10 AM||||Im looking for some little things to do to my car while im waiting for the mounts to arrive...what do you guys recommend that I can do easily and on a small budget?  I changed oil, coolant, brake pads, and cleaned out the carberator...  Anything else I can do to improve the performance of my L4 without anything major?  Right now I have problems with stalling when I start up the engine and put it in gear...I've been told Im not getting enough vacuum and I just found out my PCV valve is broken when I took off the air filter assembly...another problem is the air filter assembly and the throttle cable/shifter cable bracket is hitting the trunk...my air filter lid gets bent and exposes open air unless fixed and my cable bracket has broken off, I welded it back with an electrical welder and it broke again....so I used a gas but havent been driving it since...replacing the transmission mount and hoping that will help...the engine mount and dog bone were already replaced and im planning on getting the "ultimate dog bone" with the poly-urethane bushings.  86' SE late model with the single tranmission mount that connects to bracket...I've only been able to find that part at Fierostore.com, everywhere else asks me if I want front or rear...even if I tell them I have an 87 or 88 which has only the single mount they still ask for front or rear....  I'll post some picks of my car tomorrow when I get them off my digital camera.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-03-2000||04:37 AM||||My 2 cents....... NO POLY!!!<BR>I used a Ultimate from the Fiero Store on my 2M4 & it was a huge mistake. The car shook so much at idle , I could have rented it out as a paint shaker. 2 weeks later I bought a new stock one. <P>Check out this topic before you spend the money.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006498.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006498.html</A> <P><BR>P.S. Welcome to the Forum<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||HAGS||11-03-2000||04:41 AM||||Posting this while the other topic is loading:<P>I understand there will be more vibration, but if poly holds my engine better then thats what I need...I cant be hammering my air filter pan back into submission after every trip and I sure as heck dont want to keep welding parts back on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HAGS||11-03-2000||04:42 AM||||My brother owns an 86 GT and uses the "Ultimate" and when he let me joy ride with a V6 I didnt notice any vibrations.||||reg||1
